I have everything needed. Here is the complete report on how owner creation (POST /owners) is implemented.

## Summary

The POST endpoint is defined in an OfficeFloor YAML pipeline. The DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`) are **not** hand-written source files — they are generated at build time from `openapi.yml` by the OpenAPI generator, so I've included the schema definitions. There is **no** `findByTelephone`-style method anywhere; the only telephone logic is the `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` function (strip non-digits, require exactly 10). The existing acceptance test asserts duplicate-telephone rejection (409) but no such uniqueness check exists yet in the pipeline.

---

## 1. POST /owners pipeline YAML

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
(Note: it lives under `rest/api/owners.POST.yml`, not `rest/owners/`.)

```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

# Validate the body first so a missing or blank required field is a 400 before any
# owner is built or saved. It publishes the body for the build step to reuse.
validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwnerFields
  next: normalizeTelephone

# Strip non-digits from the telephone and require exactly 10 digits, so the owner is
# built and stored with the normalized value and a bad number is a 400.
normalizeTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.NormalizeOwnerTelephone
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```

Pipeline order: `validate` → `normalizeTelephone` → `build` → `save` → `respond`.

---

## 2. Java function classes referenced by the YAML

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Out;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerFieldsDto;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestBody;

/**
 * Rejects a create request whose required owner fields are missing or blank. Runs
 * first in the {@code POST /api/owners} pipeline so an incomplete body is a 400
 * before any owner is built or saved. It binds the body once and republishes it as
 * a variable for the later {@link BuildOwner} step.
 */
public class ValidateOwnerFields {

    public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated)
            throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
        List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
        require(missing, "firstName", request.getFirstName());
        require(missing, "lastName", request.getLastName());
        require(missing, "address", request.getAddress());
        require(missing, "city", request.getCity());
        require(missing, "telephone", request.getTelephone());
        if (!missing.isEmpty()) {
            throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
        }
        validated.set(request);
    }

    private static void require(List<String> missing, String field, String value) {
        if (value == null || value.isBlank()) {
            missing.add(field);
        }
    }
}
```

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`
