## 3. Owner entity and OwnerRepository

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`
The telephone field carries JSR-380 validation constraints:
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;

public String getTelephone() { return this.telephone; }
public void setTelephone(String telephone) { this.telephone = telephone; }
```
(Full entity extends `Person`, with `address`, `city`, `telephone`, and a `Set<Pet> pets`; standard getters/setters and `getPet(...)` helpers.)

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`
Methods (no telephone-based finder exists):
```java
Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName) throws DataAccessException;
Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable) throws DataAccessException;
Owner findById(int id) throws DataAccessException;
void save(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException;
Collection<Owner> findAll() throws DataAccessException;
Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable) throws DataAccessException;
void delete(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException;
```
I confirmed `SpringDataOwnerRepository` and `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` only implement `findByLastName` / `findById` variants — there is **no** `findByTelephone` or any telephone query anywhere in the repositories.

