---

## 6. Existing tests for owner creation

Three test files under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`:

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.acceptance;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.springframework.test.web.servlet.result.MockMvcResultMatchers.status;
import tools.jackson.databind.node.ObjectNode;

/** telephone-unique: Reject creating an owner whose normalized telephone is already used by any other owner. Re... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("telephone", a.get("telephone").asText());
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict());
	}

	@Test
	void functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone() throws Exception {
		createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
		createOwner(ownerNode()).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
	}
}
```
This asserts a duplicate normalized telephone yields **409 Conflict** — a rule that is **not yet implemented** in the current pipeline (there is no uniqueness check and no `findByTelephone`).

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`
The black-box base class (`@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser` roles `OWNER_ADMIN`/`VET_ADMIN`/`ADMIN`). Key helpers: `ownerNode()` builds a fully-valid unique owner; `uniqueTelephone()` returns `String.format("04%08d", seq())` (a 10-digit value); `createOwner()`/`createOwnerOk()` POST to `/api/owners`; `getOwner()`/`fetchOwner()` GET `/api/owners/{id}`; plus reference maps and SHA-256/Luhn helpers for anticipated derived-value rules. (Full 322-line contents read above.)

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java`
A Logback `ListAppender` helper (`AutoCloseable`) that captures events on the `AUDIT` logger so audit side-effects can be asserted. Not owner-creation-specific but used by acceptance tests.

---

## 7. Telephone normalization / "phone" logic across the codebase

- **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`** (shown above) — the only normalization logic: `request.getTelephone().replaceAll("\\D", "")`, then requires `length() == 10`, else throws `InvalidTelephoneException`. It mutates the DTO in place so the stored value is the 10-digit form.
- **`ApplyOwner.java`** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ApplyOwner.java` (used by the PUT/update path, not POST) copies fields including `owner.setTelephone(request.getTelephone())`. No normalization here.
- **`Owner.java`** — telephone `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", ...)` + `@Digits(integer = 10)`.
- **`openapi.yml`** — `OwnerFields.telephone` pattern `^[0-9]*$`, maxLength 20.
- **JDBC repos** (`JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `JdbcPetRepositoryImpl`, `JdbcVisitRepositoryImpl`) — SELECT/UPDATE the `telephone` column; no normalization or uniqueness lookup.
- **DB schemas** — `telephone VARCHAR(20)` (h2 adds `NOT NULL`); no UNIQUE constraint on telephone in any schema.

There is **no existing "normalized telephone uniqueness" check** — no `findByTelephone`, no unique index, and no query comparing normalized telephones. The `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` test expects a 409 that the current implementation does not produce.

